.TH DANBY-SOCCERKICK 1
.SH NAME
danby-soccerkick \- three-dimensional flight of a kicked soccer ball
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/soccerkick
.SH MODEL
The ball is subject to gravity, quadratic drag, and a Magnus acceleration
proportional to the cross product of spin and velocity.  Signed aim and curve
show how a kick bends independently of its vertical arc.
.SH DISPLAY
The upper graph is height versus downrange distance.  The lower graph is the
plan view, lateral displacement versus downrange distance.  Tracks alter speed,
elevation, aim, drag, curve, and gravity.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/soccerkick.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR flight3d (2)
